# Theme Builder documents

Don't add a second layout table. Theme documents are `chrome_layouts.kind`: `header` | `footer` | `body` | `single` | `archive` | `loop_item` | `overlay`.

`theme_templates` stores conditions, header/footer/body foreign keys, and `document_type`. Public cascade: record FK → matching template slot → type default → site default.

When a published single/archive body matches, render that tree; otherwise keep the coded route template as the fallback.
